  "slug": "lupus-kidney-c321",
  "summary": "Public transcriptomes are increasingly mined with WGCNA and ML panels, yet candidate signatures remain hypothesis-generating.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is discovery-stage biomarker and gene nomination from existing transcriptomic data. Most items integrate public bulk or microarray cohorts with WGCNA, LASSO, random forest, or multi-algorithm ML panels to derive gene signatures, such as the five-gene pulmonary hypertension diagnostic (AUC 0.895), the three-gene sepsis-induced acute lung injury model (AUC 0.911), and the six oxidative stress hub genes in pediatric sepsis. Several add single-cell resolution, including the 14-cell-type pulmonary hypertension map and COPD macrophage depletion with cDC2 expansion from 45,708 lung immune cells. Some layer Mendelian randomization and proteome-wide pQTL analysis onto public cohorts, as in blood proteome-wide MR for coronary artery disease and APOM prioritization in psoriasis. The diabetic macrophage preprint adds chromatin-level evidence, including 3D chromatin remodeling and enhancer-promoter rewiring. Findings remain computational and hypothesis-generating.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-14"
}
